+## First hosted exposure: writes dominate, timeout not reproduced
+
+Diagnostic head `547cb25119f518d7abd71c7e36c96423f522d0e8` passed canonical
+local validation in approximately 13m38s; unchanged push reused its receipt.
+[Run 35518511452](https://github.com/harshanandak/forge/actions/runs/35518511452)
+completed all 18 jobs. Both Windows full-matrix jobs passed; the workflow failed
+only on the separately tracked mutation source-integrity defect
+`f5d0087a-fc74-4c0d-ab1c-9621398fac0b`.
+
+| Job / case | First write | Later writes | Search | Total |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Node 22 identity | 131.980 ms | 72.534 ms | 1.875 ms | 209.291 ms |
+| Node 24 identity | 1,024.135 ms | 560.005 ms | 1.701 ms | 1,588.190 ms |
+| Node 24 single-write harness | 868.687 ms | none | 1.229 ms | 871.523 ms |
+| Node 24 foreign crowding | 840.015 ms | 2,960.666 ms | 1.696 ms | 3,807.932 ms |
+
+Both jobs use Bun 1.4.2; job labels do not establish Node-version causality.
+The original 17.65-second timeout did not recur. First write includes lazy
+database opening, schema/FTS initialization and insertion, which remain
+unseparated. Batching can reduce repeated writes but cannot explain the slow
+single-write case. The incident and merged PR verification remain open.
+
+Full content-free timing payloads and SHA-256 hashes are preserved in verified
+Kernel comments `bc399064-3b02-43a4-b43a-e1b8c7e2ff2d` and
+`03acb0a4-dfce-40ec-b122-e8b402843545`; synthesis is in
+`632ec1c3-71df-465c-adb7-742c083e737d`. Downloaded artifacts remain under
+`test-results/hosted/35518511452/node22/` and `node24/`.
+
+## Decision 5: Observe native operations through existing runtime injection
+
+Date: 2026-09-21. Task: split first-record timing. Status: RESOLVED.
+User approved continuation. Independent Sol review confirmed the existing
+`createBuiltinSQLiteDriver({ runtime })` injection and observed database wrapper
+pattern in `test/kernel/watch-owner-transaction.test.js`. Reuse that seam in the
+holdout test, without changing production code or eagerly opening the database.
+Keep the prepared batching patch unchanged. Native timing aggregates overlap
+store-level timings; they are diagnostic partitions, not additive total costs.
+
+The refinement passed the original 10 cases / 177 assertions in 7.84 seconds
+with the unchanged 15-second default. Focused ESLint exited 0. A disposable
+fake-runtime probe passed nine assertions for return/error identity, native
+receivers, lazy construction and context restoration; it was removed afterward
+so the benchmark keeps exactly its original cases. Luna's spec review passed.
+Final quality review and canonical validation are separate gates.
+
+Fresh artifact: `test-results/memory-recall-holdout-timing-17280-1789931237492.json`.
+It contains 10 cases and 16 bounded phase labels, no recording failure, negative
+durations, fixture contents or absolute paths. Host load varied during local
+measurements, so the elapsed-time difference does not establish probe overhead.
