+## Task 4: Split the dominant first-record measurement
+
+User approved continuation on 2026-09-21 after the first hosted exposure.
+Sol owns only the holdout test; root owns evidence, review and publication.
+Use the driver's existing `options.runtime` injection and the real selected
+database class to observe open, exec, prepare and statement execution. Preserve
+lazy initialization, runtime selection, constructor options, native receivers,
+returns and errors. Keep the original store-level measurements for comparison.
+Only stable phase names, counts and durations may be retained; nested native
+timings overlap store timings and must not be added together.
+
+No eager initialization, global patching, production changes, fixture batching,
+timeout changes or workflow changes. Retain all 10 cases and 177 assertions.
+Run focused tests, lint and a small return/error/receiver probe; obtain spec then
+quality review. Commit, run one canonical validation, reuse its receipt on push,
+and capture one hosted exposure of the changed diagnostic experiment. Preserve
+the findings without calling a passing exposure a reliability repair.
